         "step": 1,
         "text": "Complete the square in the quadratic: \\( x^{2} - 6 x + 13 = \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2} + 4 \\).",
         "rule_named": "completing the square"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The integrand has the shape of an inverse trigonometric derivative, \\( \\frac{d}{dx} \\arctan\\left(\\frac{x - 3}{2}\\right) = \\frac{2}{4 + \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "antiderivative read from a derivative rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "With \\( u = \\frac{x - 3}{2}, \\; dx = 2\\,du \\), the integral becomes \\( \\int \\frac{10}{4\\left(1 + u^{2}\\right)} \\cdot 2\\,du = 5 \\int \\frac{du}{1 + u^{2}} \\), which is \\( 5 \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{3}{2} \\right)} + C \\).",
